-06-23T20:46:41Z","closed_at":"2026-06-23T19:55:12Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119319","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119319","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119319.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119319.patch","merged_at":"2026-06-23T19:55:12Z"},"body":"Salvaging of #112327 with some modifications.\r\n\r\nAdds `MeshLibrary` item categories that are shown in a category tree view in the `GridMap` editor:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"840\" height=\"380\" alt=\"gridmap_categories\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/44239e5d-35f7-4bb2-9ac0-da0bc8426d15\" />\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n- `MeshLibrary` items have a new property called `category`, which can be used create categories (and sub categories using `/` as a delimiter).\r\n- In the `GridMap` editor, a tree will show up if any categories are found. Category names will be taken into account when filtering items.\r\n\r\n- ~The delimiter for sub categories can be set with `MeshLibrary.category_delimiter`, with options for slashes, compound words, and snake case.~\r\n- ~Categories can be created automatically if `MeshLibrary.categorize_by_name` is enabled.~\r\n- ~When exporting a scene to a `MeshLibrary`, it will autofill item categories if the `MeshInstance3D`s contain the metadata \"category\" with a `String` value.~\r\n\r\nSee discussion below.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gis